# I use PC shutdown to notify me that it is a time to take a break/finish the
# work for the day and to make it difficult to break the habit of keeping a
# consistent daily schedule.
#
# Advantages:
#      1. I have to stop what I was doing.
#
#	   I could use alarm, but my issue with alarms was, that alarms can go
#	   unnoticed (e.g. if sound is muted) and are easy to postpone. Postponing
#	   is however not a good practice for building strong habits. If I need to
#	   finish some work, I can turn the PC back on for a minute (shutdown uses
#	   "+1m" as the default time parameter), which is enough time to finish my
#	   work and save files.
#
#      2. I don't have to think about turning off the PC and can just always
#      leave it on.
#
#      3. It forces me to context switch, by closing all my open apps (my
#      desktop is then less cluttered during the day) and helps me to
#      reevaluate my priorities for the day during breaks (it takes me at least
#      15min to "unfocus" from the thing I was doing until I am able to do some
#      planning). I.e. it helps me to distinguish between important and "nice to
#      have" tasks by giving me some perspective and time to do/reevaluate my
#      daily/weekly planning.
#
#      4. Optionally I can also add alarm on my phone for 10 minutes before the
#      shutdown timer, so that I am not surprised by the shutdown.
#
#      TODO - what if I will be having an online call or teaching? TOSOLVE

# 6:45 wake up & hydrate & low intensity exercise (stretching and a few
# push-ups), morning routine
# 7:00 high intensity exercise & sunlight (run, push ups, strength training)
# ~7:45 - breakfast
# ~8:00 - planning of the next 3 days (including this one)
# 8:00 - 9:00 - communication i.e. WA & shallow focus work for the day
# 9:00 - 9:15 "terce" small pause to pray & think about priorities for the day
0-15   9      * * *  root /sbin/shutdown

# 9:15 - 11:45 First deep work session (phone off)

# preparation for lunch & lunch
45-59  11     * * *  root /sbin/shutdown
*      12     * * *  root /sbin/shutdown

# 13:00 - 15:30 second deep focus session

# 15:30 - 15:50 a pause to slow down revisit my day & context switch if needed
30-50  15     * * *  root /sbin/shutdown

# 16:00 - 19:15 third deep work session

# 19:15 - 8:00 - "great silence" i.e. preparations for sleep, relax & sleep
15-59  19     * * *  root /sbin/shutdown
*      20-23  * * *  root /sbin/shutdown
*      0-7    * * *  root /sbin/shutdown


